# Introduction to Rust Integration

Lux provides robust support for integrating with Rust, allowing developers to seamlessly work with Rust-compatible types and perform conversions between Elixir and Rust.

## Creating a Rust Struct

To create a Rust struct using Lux, you can define a new module with the `defmodule` macro and specify the fields using `defstruct`.

defmodule Lux.Rust.MyStruct do
  @moduledoc "Rust-compatible struct"

  defstruct [:field1, :field2]

  def new(field1, field2) do
    %__MODULE__{field1: field1, field2: field2}
  end

  def to_rust_field1(%__MODULE__{field1: value}) do
    :erlang.nif_call(:rust_nifs, :to_rust_field1, [value])
  end

  def from_rust_field1(rust_value) do
    :erlang.nif_call(:rust_nifs, :from_rust_field1, [rust_value])
  end

  def to_rust_field2(%__MODULE__{field2: value}) do
    :erlang.nif_call(:rust_nifs, :to_rust_field2, [value])
  end

  def from_rust_field2(rust_value) do
    :erlang.nif_call(:rust_nifs, :from_rust_field2, [rust_value])
  end
end

## Converting to and from Rust

To convert an Elixir value to a Rust-compatible format, use the `to_rust` function. To convert a Rust-compatible value back to Elixir, use the `from_rust` function.

rust_struct = Lux.Rust.MyStruct.new("value1", "value2")
rust_value = Lux.Rust.MyStruct.to_rust_field1(rust_struct)
elixir_value = Lux.Rust.MyStruct.from_rust_field1(rust_value)

## Using the `deftype` Macro

The `deftype` macro simplifies the creation of Rust-compatible structs by generating the necessary functions automatically.

defmodule Lux.Rust.AutoStruct do
  deftype AutoStruct, [:field1, :field2]
end

rust_struct = Lux.Rust.AutoStruct.new("value1", "value2")
rust_value = Lux.Rust.AutoStruct.to_rust_field1(rust_struct)
elixir_value = Lux.Rust.AutoStruct.from_rust_field1(rust_value)

## Converting Between Elixir and Rust

To convert an Elixir value to a Rust-compatible format, use the `elixir_to_rust/1` function. To convert a Rust-compatible value back to Elixir, use the `rust_to_elixir/1` function.

elixir_struct = %Lux.Rust.MyStruct{field1: "value1", field2: "value2"}
rust_value = Lux.Rust.elixir_to_rust(elixir_struct)
elixir_value = Lux.Rust.rust_to_elixir(rust_value)

These examples demonstrate how to work with Rust-compatible types in Lux, including manual struct creation and automatic struct generation using the `deftype` macro.
